WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>Thanks for making the time. Is the door shut your end?

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:10.667
<v Clementine Treadwell>Yeah, I'm in one of sort of, the little um, booths. The ones with no air.

00:00:10.867 --> 00:00:22.400
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>Ha, I know them well. Right. So, as I said sort of, in my message, this um, is a confidential conversation. I'll keep notes but they'll stay in the case file.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.333
<v Clementine Treadwell>Understood.

00:00:24.533 --> 00:00:29.467
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>So. You wanted sort of, to raise something about your team.

00:00:29.667 --> 00:01:00.200
<v Clementine Treadwell>Yes. Okay. sort of, Um. So I'll just say it. One of my team, Wilhelmina Adebanjo-Whitlow, came to me last week and said that Peregrina Wainscott has been making comments about her, you know, about her appearance, and messaging her late at night, and it's been going on since the conference in the spring. And she was really upset, like really upset, and she asked uh, me not to do anything, but I don't think I can just not do anything? Can I?

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:04.400
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>No, you did the right thing um, coming to us.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:08.000
<v Clementine Treadwell>Okay. Good. Because I haven't slept.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:13.133
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>I understand. Can I sort of, ask, where was the conference?

00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:22.467
<v Clementine Treadwell>It was in Harrowfield, at the sort of, big hotel by the station. And then um, there was a dinner in Lake Orrin afterwards.

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:24.933
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>And were you there?

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:32.533
<v Clementine Treadwell>I was at the conference, not at the dinner. I left early to get the train back uh, to Sheffield.

00:01:32.733 --> 00:01:36.733
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>Okay. And has anyone else witnessed anything?

00:01:36.933 --> 00:01:50.600
<v Clementine Treadwell>She thinks Lucinda might have seen some of uh, the messages. And, um, I think there may have been a similar complaint about him at his last company, someone mentioned it at the Christmas do.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:55.600
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>Okay. I'll note that as hearsay, you know, but thank you.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.133
<v Clementine Treadwell>Sure.

00:01:57.333 --> 00:02:00.867
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>Now, how is she? Is she at like, work?

00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:03.933
<v Clementine Treadwell>She's been off since Monday.

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:10.800
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>Sorry, I'll rephrase, can I ask if there's any health element we need to be aware of?

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:21.800
<v Clementine Treadwell>She's been under the doctor for anxiety for a while, and this has knocked her back quite badly, she said she's had a few panic attacks at her desk.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:34.400
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>Okay. That's really important uh, for us to know, for the support side. We can refer her to occupational health, and the employee assistance line is open around the clock.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:38.667
<v Clementine Treadwell>What's the number? I'd like to give it to her.

00:02:38.867 --> 00:02:47.000
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>It's 675-555-0185. And I'd suggest she emails me directly as well, at matthias_brackenridge@quenby.example.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.267
<v Clementine Treadwell>Okay. Thank you.

00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:54.267
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>Now. A couple of process things. Is he still in the team?

00:02:54.467 --> 00:02:59.200
<v Clementine Treadwell>Yes. That's the awful bit. He sits about two desks away.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:12.467
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>Right. We'll look at whether we can move him temporarily, maybe basically, to the Little Hatherby office, or the hot desks at Tannery Yard. um, That won't be framed as a punishment.

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:14.000
<v Clementine Treadwell>Okay.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:23.933
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>Can I um, ask, sorry, um, this is a bit indirect, but is there anything about his performance or his contract we should know about?

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:30.600
<v Clementine Treadwell>Well. He's on a performance plan already, actually. His numbers have been about...

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.200
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>Go on.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:47.467
<v Clementine Treadwell>His numbers have been about forty percent of target for two quarters. And the team's attrition, I mean, honestly, we've lost a third of the team this year and I'm now basically, wondering if this is part of why.

00:03:47.667 --> 00:04:00.267
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>Mm. That's um, a fair question. For what it's worth, exit interviews flag a sort of, manager issue in maybe one in five cases across the whole business, so it's worth asking.

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:06.533
<v Clementine Treadwell>And I know the business is, um, I know there's a restructure coming in Q1...

00:04:06.733 --> 00:04:09.333
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>I can't comment on that.

00:04:09.533 --> 00:04:12.000
<v Clementine Treadwell>No, I um, know. Sorry.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:19.333
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>But, for what it's worth, any outcome here is separate from that. I want to be really clear.

00:04:19.533 --> 00:04:21.200
<v Clementine Treadwell>Okay. Yes.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:32.933
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>So, next steps. I'll open a case, the reference will be AC787533848. I'll speak to her first, with her consent. Then we'll decide on I mean, an investigation.

00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:36.467
<v Clementine Treadwell>Will he like, know it came from me?

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:43.933
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>We'll do our best. I can't promise anonymity you know, entirely, but we'll be I mean, careful.

00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:49.133
<v Clementine Treadwell>Okay. Thank you. Honestly. This is the worst bit of the job.

00:04:49.333 --> 00:04:53.400
<v Ilsabet Strathairn>It really is. You're doing fine. Speak Friday?

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.667
<v Clementine Treadwell>Friday. basically, Yes. Thanks.
